  "text" : "Now the moment that makes this land, the one I'd show you first, if I only had thirty seconds.\nSame rule everywhere, encrypt data at rest.\nSame real risk number behind it, £21,107.\nComputed identically every time.\nThree institutions, one control.\nWatch what the pounds decide when the tolerance changes underneath it.\nDriftwoods tolerance is forty thousand pounds, twenty one thousand fits.\nSo the control audits\nLudlow holding decades of confidential health data has a 5,000 pound tolerance.\nThe same 21,000 blows straight through it, so the control denies.\nTuppence at 15,000 denies two.\nOne rule.\nOne number three verdicts, driven entirely by risk appetite, not by opinion.\nAnd it's never just yes or no, fall behind on patching and your workload still runs caged\nFewer capabilities, tighter limits, watched harder, more expensive to operate.\nThat's the real borderline.\nTotal cost of risk.\nIt's the risk you're keeping plus the cost of every control.\nRight now on this book that's £47,921, staying current is provably the cheaper path."
